# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREDENTIALS — never commit. This repository is PUBLIC.
#
# A Telethon .session file is a post-authentication BEARER CREDENTIAL: it
# grants full API access to the Telegram account (read every chat, send as
# that account) and bypasses both the account password and 2FA. It is revoked
# only by explicitly terminating the session from another device.
#
# An MT5 master password grants full trading control of the account from any
# terminal, anywhere. MT5 has no scoped API keys.
#
# A push to a public repo cannot be undone: unreachable git objects stay
# retrievable by SHA, forks make them permanent, and the public Events API
# archives the push. Secret-scraping bots index public pushes within minutes.
# If one of these is ever committed, rotate the credential — do not just
# delete the file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Telegram (Telethon / Pyrogram)
*.session
*.session-journal
*.session_string
anon.session*

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Local / real configuration. Commit only sanitised examples.
config/local.yaml
config/local.yml
config/*.local.yaml
config/secrets.yaml
mt5_credentials*
terminal.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA — the trading ledger and the message archive.
#
# The archive holds third-party message content and images with no retention
# basis, and it grows without bound. Keep both out of the repo, and keep the
# archive on a different volume from the ledger so a full archive disk cannot
# stop the ledger from recording losses (which would stop the kill switch from
# ever tripping).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
media/
archive/
corpus/
*.jsonl

# Model / eval outputs
eval_runs/
.prompt_cache/

